    '**Rule 4.** _"A second officer must see the identification for any cash withdrawal above 500,000, **and for any second withdrawal by the same customer on the same day at this counter, whatever the amounts.** Where the cashier cannot establish whether an earlier withdrawal was made today, **the second-officer check applies.** **Purpose: that no large sum leaves against a document only one person has seen.**"_',
    '_Four things make Rule 4 work. It names a test the cashier can perform. It **resolves the unknown case in favour of the check** rather than leaving it to judgement. It does not reach for information the counter does not have. And it states its purpose, so a cashier facing a fifth case can reason from it._',
