  wTask: { brief: 'Write a testable standard for your own area, with its measurement and its breach action.', words: '150 to 250 words',
    sample: ['**REMITTANCE DESK STANDARD 1 · payout time · issued 10 April · supersedes the desk note of June 2024**',
             '**The standard.** **No beneficiary who arrives with a reference number and an identity document will leave without being paid or given a time.**',
             '**Measurement.** From the moment the beneficiary reaches the desk to the moment cash is counted into their hand, or a written time is given to them. **Not from when they entered the branch.**',
             '**Who tests it, and when.** The paying clerk, at the desk, at the moment the beneficiary is about to leave. **Nothing is calculated and nothing is reported upward to be measured.**',
             '**What happens when it cannot be met.** The clerk calls the desk supervisor, who will either **(a)** authorise the payout under the exception clause, or **(b)** write the beneficiary a time and a named contact on a slip. **One of the two must happen. "Come back tomorrow" without a slip is not an option.**',
             '**Why not a minutes target.** The June 2024 note said "payouts within eight minutes". **It was breached every time the system was slow, which was most of February, and no breach ever produced anything. A standard about the outcome the beneficiary cares about — leaving with money or with a time — can be met on every day of the year.**'] },
